### **1. Impact of 0.25 dB Passband Loss on Link Budget Margins**
A 0.25 dB passband loss in the receiver's front-end significantly reduces the available signal power, which directly impacts the link budget margins. This reduction in signal power can limit the achievable data rates and reduce the reliability of the link. For instance, if the receiver cannot handle the reduced signal strength, it may struggle to transmit data effectively, leading to lower link margins and potential link reliability issues.

