The key insight is that the defocused reflector generally has a slightly reduced gain after MVDR beamforming compared to the conventional reflector. This reduction is particularly evident in the direction of the dropped out feed elements. The conventional reflector antenna would be severely handicapped without redundancy concepts or adequate margin in terms of SNR. Therefore, the optimal spacing should maximize the pattern optimization with specific goals and constraints, such as minimizing pattern sidelobes while maintaining the gain in the desired cell.

