One potential approach is to incorporate adaptive beamforming algorithms that can dynamically adjust the beam patterns based on the current flight path and aircraft configuration. This adaptive strategy could use machine learning algorithms to predict the likely flight path and adjust the beamforming parameters accordingly. Additionally, the use of advanced signal processing techniques, such as network coding, could help to improve the reliability and capacity of the communication links. 

Another promising technology is the implementation of dynamic beamforming schemes that can adapt to the spatial non-stationary characteristics of the channel, such as visibility regions where the channel energy is significant. These schemes could help to mitigate the impact of spatial non-stationarity on the performance of beam space multiplexing schemes. 

